Subject: [PATCH] avformat/dvdvideodec: enable libdvdnav read-ahead

With read-ahead disabled, libdvdnav fetches one 2048-byte sector per
dvdnav_get_next_block() call. Disc images hide this behind the OS page cache,
but a physical drive opened through the raw device (as libdvdread does for CSS)
then sees one command per sector: ~240 IOPS, ~0.46 MB/s on a USB DVD drive.

dvdvideodec uses the copying dvdnav_get_next_block() API, which is correct with
the read cache on. Enabling it lets libdvdnav issue reads of up to 512 sectors:
measured 2.6 MB/s on the same drive and disc (drive maximum: 3.4 MB/s), a ~5.5x
speedup for real-disc demuxing. Output is byte-identical.
---
--- a/libavformat/dvdvideodec.c
+++ b/libavformat/dvdvideodec.c
@@ -533,7 +533,7 @@
 
     if (!state->dvdnav                                                          ||
         dvdnav_open_status != DVDNAV_STATUS_OK                                  ||
-        dvdnav_set_readahead_flag(state->dvdnav, 0) != DVDNAV_STATUS_OK         ||
+        dvdnav_set_readahead_flag(state->dvdnav, 1) != DVDNAV_STATUS_OK         ||
         dvdnav_set_PGC_positioning_flag(state->dvdnav, 1) != DVDNAV_STATUS_OK   ||
         dvdnav_get_region_mask(state->dvdnav, &disc_region_mask) != DVDNAV_STATUS_OK) {
 
